      "start": 300,
      "details": "<p>The name \"Centenarium Aqua Frigida\" is attested in an honorific Latin inscription executed during the reign of Diocletian. The text names a man of the equestrian order by the name of Titus Aurelius Litua. Munzi et al. 2014 suggests the text should be dated to 293 CE.</p>",
